WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.975
Here's the answer in
brief, in five points.

2
00:00:02.975 --> 00:00:09.912
First, a G M S A or a D M S A is a better
password, not a Zero Trust identity.

3
00:00:09.912 --> 00:00:13.823
It removes the password a person knows,
which is the Kerberoasting risk,

4
00:00:13.823 --> 00:00:18.199
but the workload still authenticates
with Kerberos against Active Directory.

5
00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:22.570
Nothing in Entra I D evaluates that
sign-in, so Conditional Access,

6
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:26.050
Entra's risk signals and the
sign-in logs never see it.

7
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:31.208
Second, a Microsoft Entra workload identity
moves the identity into the program's

8
00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:33.863
central store, with no
secret anyone holds,

9
00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:38.869
a managed identity or a federated credential,
or with a short-lived certificate,

10
00:00:38.869 --> 00:00:41.600
and every token it gets
is logged in Entra I D.

11
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.237
The limit, from Microsoft Learn:
Conditional Access for workload identities

12
00:00:46.237 --> 00:00:50.512
covers single-tenant service principals
only, not managed identities.

13
00:00:50.512 --> 00:00:55.563
Third, SASE protects the people in front
of a service, not the service itself.

14
00:00:55.563 --> 00:01:00.071
Private Access and application proxy
put Entra sign-in and phishing-resistant

15
00:01:00.071 --> 00:01:03.760
multifactor authentication in
front of a Kerberos application,

16
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.312
then reach it with Kerberos
constrained delegation to its S P N.

17
00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:11.156
The application's own service account
and S P N stay where they are,

18
00:01:11.156 --> 00:01:14.287
and service-to-service
traffic doesn't go through the

19
00:01:14.287 --> 00:01:17.775
Global Secure Access client,
which runs on end-user devices.

20
00:01:17.775 --> 00:01:20.700
Fourth, certificates
change shape, not count.

21
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.079
Fifth, extend Entra I D for
people across every cloud,

22
00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:27.300
but don't force one workload
identity across them.

23
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.180
That last one is the program's
recommendation, design guidance.
